/T (   The rapid expansion of microtonal music during the twentieth and twenty-first centuries has generated an extraordinary diversity of tuning systems, compositional approaches, and experimental instruments. However, this development has also revealed a fundamental problem that remains unresolved: the absence of a universal and standardized system for the reading and writing of microintervals.)
/E (   The rapid expansion of microtonal music during the twentieth and twenty-first centuries has generated an extraordinary diversity of tuning systems, compositional approaches, and experimental instruments. However, this development has also revealed a fundamental problem that remains unresolved: the absence of a universal and standardized system for the reading and writing of microintervals.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [7]
>>
