/Title (This lecture-recital explores the artistic and practical integration of Arabic maqam traditions into contemporary jazz through the use of a quarter-tone piano. While microtonality has been widely discussed in relation to composition and tuning theory, its implementation within jazz improvisation on fixed-pitch Western instruments remains relatively rare. The presentation examines how a quarter-tone piano can function as a bridge between the modal language of Arabic music and the improvisational practices of jazz.)
